---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import Callout from '../components/Callout.astro';
import Cta from '../components/Cta.astro';
import { links } from '../config/links';
import { site } from '../config/site';

const title = 'Complaints and concerns';
const lead =
  'How to raise a concern about conduct in the Society’s activities, or about how the Society itself has acted.';
---

<Page title={title} eyebrow="Governance" lead={lead}>
  <p class="lead">
    A professional body is only as good as its willingness to hear when something has gone wrong.
    Concerns are treated seriously and confidentially.
  </p>

  <h2>What this covers</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Conduct in the Society's activities — meetings, online forums, events, publications and
      committee work — that falls short of the
      {' '}<a href="/participation-code/">member participation code</a>.
    </li>
    <li>Decisions or conduct of the Society itself, including its committee.</li>
    <li>
      How the Society has handled your personal information (see also the
      {' '}<a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a>).
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How to raise a concern</h2>
  <p>
    Concerns about conduct may be raised with the Secretary or the President. Write to
    {' '}<a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>, marking your message for their attention, and
    include:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>what happened, and when;</li>
    <li>who was involved, if you are comfortable saying;</li>
    <li>any relevant correspondence or materials; and</li>
    <li>what outcome you are seeking.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    <Cta href={links.complaints} variant="primary">Raise a concern</Cta>
  </p>

  <h2>How concerns are handled</h2>
  <p>
    Concerns are handled by the committee fairly, confidentially and in accordance with the
    association's rules. Committee members with a conflict of interest in the matter step back from
    considering it.
  </p>
  <p>
    Serious or repeated breaches of the member participation code may lead to action under the rules,
    including suspension or termination of membership.
  </p>

  <Callout tone="pending" title="Being finalised">
    <p>
      A fuller complaints procedure is in preparation and will be published here. It will set out who
      receives complaints, how conflicts of interest are managed, what procedural fairness applies,
      the possible outcomes or sanctions, and whether there is an appeal process.
    </p>
  </Callout>

  <h2>If you are not satisfied</h2>
  <p>
    The rules provide a process for resolving disputes between members, and between members and the
    Society. For concerns specifically about personal information, you may lodge a complaint with the
    Office of the Australian Information Commissioner at
    {' '}<a href="https://www.oaic.gov.au" rel="noopener">oaic.gov.au</a>, or with the relevant data
    protection authority in your jurisdiction.
  </p>

  <h2>Urgent safety concerns</h2>
  <p>
    If someone is at immediate risk of harm, contact your local emergency services first. Write to us
    afterwards so we can act on our side.
  </p>
</Page>
